# The Quota slice: the start, the class, the wide lens at dawn. Story lead, 2026-10-21.

# The cold open (design/spine-plan/02-WITNESS.md section 1, revision 12): forty seconds of Anni's kitchen years
# later, before the day. The player plays the day not knowing which of the children is missing from her life.
# Game director, 2026-10-22.
@node q.start
place: q_anni_room
cost: 0
camera: near
nar: A kitchen, a long time after. A tin on the oilcloth with the lid off, and a girl of about twelve taking the papers out of it one at a time and laying them in a row.
line: DAUGHTER: What's all these?
line: ANNI: Put them back the way they were. They go in order.
nar: The woman at the stove has a long careful face, and a blue thread round her wrist so old it has gone the colour of string.
line: DAUGHTER: Of what, though?
nar: Anni comes over and puts the lid on the tin, and keeps her hand flat on it.
line: ANNI: Ask me when you're older.
go: q.start.class

@node q.start.class
place: q_tower
cost: 0
# the class carries over from era 1 (coordinator, under the blanket approval, 2026-10-23): Abel's line is Ned's, Josh's is Will's
alt: e1.carry.ned ? q_class == inspector
alt: e1.carry.will ? q_class == militia
nar: Winter. Edrin, the Upper Town.
nar: Whose day is it?
opt: "Ned Furrowe. District inspector. He signs the returns." -> q.wide {do: q_class = inspector; become(q.ned)}
opt: "Will Brack. Sergeant of militia. He keeps the cells and the road post." -> q.wide {do: q_class = militia; become(q.will)}

@node q.wide
place: q_tower
cost: 10
do: record(export.train, haldane, haldane_yard); shift(export, 1)
camera: wide
nar: From the bell tower, before it is light. Frost on the slates of Exchange Street, and smoke from about one chimney in four.
nar: The relief queue starts at the office door and goes round three sides of the square. People stand close for the warmth. Nobody talks. A woman near the back is holding a child who is too big to be held, and every so often she shifts him to the other hip.
nar: On the fourth side, under the lamps of the goods yard, the export train. Soldiers stand along it with their rifles slung while men load sacks stencilled HALVARD GRAIN CO. In the queue, heads turn to watch every sack go up, and turn back.
nar: Past the church, on the hill's shoulder, the burial ground. The new rows are on the left, where the ground was soft enough to dig in October. Since the frost they have been leaving the coffins in the church porch.
go: q.wide.man

# the same view, as the man the player chose; the player steps down from it by choice
@node q.wide.man
cost: 0
alt: q.wide.ned ? q_class == inspector
go: q.wide.will

@node q.wide.ned
place: q_tower
cost: 3
camera: wide
nar: On the far side of the square, on the first floor over the relief office, the returns-room window, dark. The queue starts directly under it. Ned Furrowe has stood at that window most mornings this winter with his coffee and has never once looked straight down.
voice: sum: You could count them from here, if you wanted the figure. You go down the back stairs. {dc: 3}
opt: "Go down to the returns room." -> q.morning

@node q.wide.will
place: q_tower
cost: 3
camera: wide
nar: West, the post road going out across the plain in a straight line, white, to the district line and the hut. You can see the brazier's smoke from here if you know where to look.
nar: And under the office, at the height of the queue's boots, the barred lights of the cells. People stand on the gratings because they're warmer.
voice: grip: Your hand's in your pocket, on the bread. {dc: 2}
opt: "Go down to the cells." -> q.morning

@node q.morning
cost: 0
alt: q.ned.morning ? q_class == inspector
go: q.will.morning
